SECTION 1: TEAM WORKING AGREEMENT

Core Communication & Collaboration
Communication channels: Primary team communication takes place in designated project channels; urgent blockers are flagged directly to the Scrum Master.
Response times: Team members respond to project queries within core working hours.
Daily Syncs & Standups: Regular status updates are posted covering what was completed, what is next, and any blockers.
Respect & Openness: Constructive feedback is encouraged, and team decisions are made collaboratively.

Version Control & Workflow Standards
Branching strategy: Feature branches are created from main following standard naming conventions.
Commit guidelines: Commits must be clear, concise, and linked to specific task IDs.
Pull Request policy: Direct commits to protected branches are strictly prohibited. Every PR requires at least one approval before merging.

SECTION 2: DEFINITION OF DONE (DoD)

Code & Feature Completion
Functional requirements: All user story acceptance criteria are fully met and verified.
Code quality: Code is clean, documented where necessary, and follows established team coding standards.
Self-review: Developers complete a thorough self-review before opening a Pull Request.

Testing & Integration
Testing: Unit, integration, or manual test cases pass successfully without breaking existing features.
Build status: Application builds cleanly without console errors or critical warnings.
PR Approval: The PR is reviewed, approved by designated reviewers, and merged into the target branch.

Documentation & Task Tracking
Task Status: The corresponding task on the project board and task plan spreadsheet is updated to Merged or Done with the PR link attached.

SECTION 3: ROLE GUIDE & RESPONSIBILITIES

Scrum Master (SM)
Facilitates sprint ceremonies, maintains the project board, removes team blockers, and enforces repository protection and governance rules.

Developer (DEV)
Implements feature requirements, writes clean and maintainable code, creates pull requests adhering to PR templates, and resolves review feedback.

Database Administrator (DBA)
Designs and maintains the database schema, writes seed scripts, creates required views/triggers, and ensures query performance and integrity.

Tester / QA (TST)
Drafts test plans and test cases, performs feature and regression testing, logs structured bug reports, and verifies fixes before final release.

UI/UX Designer (UIX)
Creates color palettes, typography guidelines, wireframes, and high-fidelity mockups, ensuring the built interface matches design specs.

SECTION 4: DEFINITION OF DONE (SCRUM MASTER CHECKLIST)

Team Working Agreement is documented and agreed upon by all team members.
Definition of Done criteria are finalized and established across all project roles.
Role Guide detailing specific responsibilities for SM, DEV, DBA, TST, and UIX is published.
Task status for S1-SM-03 is updated to Merged / Done in the task plan spreadsheet with the documentation PR link attached.
